[00:14.68]Just eighteen when I left home
[00:24.75]Looking at mountains through the train window, I thought I left for good
[00:35.47]I worked day in and day out
[00:40.49]For the burning dream of youth
[00:45.88]Believed as long as I ran fast enough
[00:50.44]I could've caught the truth
[00:56.48]From the Ula Mountains to Ürümchi
[01:01.97]Then from east to west
[01:07.18]Two days and three nights on the green train
[01:12.18]But my station went right past
[01:47.63]I fell in love with a gal
[01:52.91]But she never knew how
[01:57.62]At the corner of East Street
[02:02.69]For the first time I fell down
[02:08.72]I headed south with empty pockets
[02:13.99]My ticket paid for by a friend
[02:19.23]Carrying my beloved guitar
[02:23.72]And a suitcase to the end
[02:30.05]Took the ferry cross the Yangtze.
[02:35.26]Then passed the banks of river Huai
[02:40.59]Singing from dusk to dawn
[02:45.07]And never asking why
[03:21.03]I had a taste of freedom, with my spirits high
[03:31.35]Sometimes, to make a living, you've gotta find your way
[03:42.09]I knocked a man down
[03:47.28]For the tricks he liked to play.
[03:52.79]I believed what is trustworthy
[03:57.42]And never cared for less
[04:04.16]I indulged in drinking and parties.
[04:08.73]And hardly thought of what is best
[04:13.91]People say that those who go their own way
[04:18.57]Will have a debt to pay
[04:54.51]At last, I lost my freedom
[04:58.09]And with it lost her, too
[05:04.71]She said that she would wait for me
[05:09.15]But only for a sec
[05:15.44]From Liverpool to Haikou
[05:20.63]Found them again and again
[05:25.84]Heard that she and the child
[05:30.65]Had settled down in the end
[05:36.86]On the road home
[05:42.08]It was long and full of strife
[05:47.42]I set off at dawn
[05:51.73]But have yet to arrive
[05:58.16]A hard and heavy snow
[06:03.39]Upon my shoulders it does fall
[06:08.74]In the stream of steel and wheel
[06:13.02]My tears are raining through it all
